<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Rhode</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.) · capital Rhode</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Greek colony at Roses on the Catalan coast, linked to Emporion and Massalia, whose silver coins bore a rose.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ancient writers credited Rhode to settlers from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rhodes">Rhodes</a>, but archaeology shows a Greek settlement founded in the 5th to 4th century BCE, probably by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massalia">Massalia</a> or nearby <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emporion">Emporion</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-roses">Gulf of Roses</a> in north-east <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Catalonia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Rhode was a small Greek trading town with its own pottery workshops. In the 3rd century BCE it minted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> drachms showing a rose, a pun on its name, widely copied in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. Excavations in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciutadella-de-roses">Ciutadella of Roses</a> have uncovered its houses and streets.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>During the north-eastern revolt of 195 BCE Rhode was held against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and was captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cato-the-elder">Cato</a>. It continued as a small town under Roman rule, later giving its name to Roses.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 400 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:4.08%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rhode</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Spain</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rhoda, Roses</dd></dl></aside></div>
